#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068472 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068685 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7229f1d0-4ba7-50ff-b5be-5697c886a175" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Compound Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "0901e241-519b-50ee-ab5f-50b2f631e948" :question/math-academy-id "e-13932" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $0 \\leq 3x+6 < 15.$" :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t0 &\\leq 3x+6 < 15 \\[5pt]\n\t0 - 6 &\\leq 3x + 6 -6 < 15-6 \\[5pt]\n\t-6 &\\leq 3x < 9 \\[5pt]\n\t\\dfrac{-6}{3} &\\leq \\dfrac{3x}{3} < \\dfrac{9}{3} \\[5pt]\n\t-2 &\\leq x < 3\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-2 \\leq x < 3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068473 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068686 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5930113e-6971-59c9-810a-97fd25bc4f89" :knowledge-point/title "Compound Inequalities That Require Flipping the Inequality Sign"}] :question/id #uuid "8208b5ba-8c54-5c05-a9f4-04aa30f8892f" :question/math-academy-id "e-13933" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-1 < -2x + 1 \\leq 7.$" :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & <-2x+1\\le 7 \\\\ -1-1 & <-2x+1-1\\le 7-1 \\\\ -2 & <-2x\\le 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we need to divide by $-2$. However, because we are dividing by a negative, we also need to flip the inequality signs.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & <-2x\\le 6 \\\\ \\frac{-2}{-2} & \\,>\\,\\frac{-2x}{-2}\\,\\ge \\,\\frac{6}{-2} \\\\ 1 & >x\\ge -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution can be written as $1 > x \\geq - 3,$ but this is somewhat difficult to read because the larger number is on the left rather than the right. So, we will rewrite the solution by reversing the order of the numbers:\n\n$$\n-3 \\leq x < 1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068474 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068687 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3ff37f0-6e45-5da4-ac87-1b93c8df3e80" :knowledge-point/title "Representing Solutions of Compound Inequalities on Number Lines"}] :question/id #uuid "7f671658-055a-599d-8f1f-416570e604b6" :question/math-academy-id "e-13935" :question/problem "Represent the solution to the inequality $-3 < 1-2x < 11$ using a number line." :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual. \n\nFirst, we apply the addition principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3 & <1-2x<11 \\\\ -3-1 & <1-2x-1<11-1 \\\\ -4 & <-2x<10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $-2.$ Note that since we are dividing by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality signs. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4 & <-2x<10 \\\\ \\frac{-4}{-2} & >\\frac{-2x}{-2}>\\frac{10}{-2} \\\\ 2 & >x>-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution can be written as $2 > x > -5$, but this is somewhat difficult to read because the larger number is on the left rather than the right. So, we will rewrite the solution by reversing the order of the numbers: \n\n$$\n-5 < x < 2\n$$\n\nWe can represent this solution using a number line, as follows.\n\n![](images/f5/f514a2aca3b3995ea2b1dc970a3b8f16a476ec0f9bb0178909d86ff670503354.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507497 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068687 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3ff37f0-6e45-5da4-ac87-1b93c8df3e80" :knowledge-point/title "Representing Solutions of Compound Inequalities on Number Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "267c3672-d4fa-528a-a9d8-0a084b2f4441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/88/88ee03f8c7f3d38bc14e3df111fc47a94e56b12e76722c39241d418d3fae4e77.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506766} {:answer/id #uuid "5f49e2f2-33dd-52a6-abda-36353b9efa9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e8/e8cc882e0c790241fa138aebf88318e6959edfb51c0a10cc7175392db3841cfb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506907} {:answer/id #uuid "c156ad87-8e71-527b-b388-ea7785312644" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/76/7648bfe90dee18fd2f91058dcf5861b69cbc6f314689fb6277da935490b5aab1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507104} {:answer/id #uuid "e55b16de-d537-5aad-887c-c53c5a94b62f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3c/3c17bd753a4a017caea2942fdf2928157a414fd1f4b8bfe4a6274c3a52efb139.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507180} {:answer/id #uuid "fd3f8f4e-6a2d-543c-9385-669d33cf8d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1c/1c69a6e3100dc342416977ad266431fd198d0335b583200ad0ab067d4786cd1f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e55b16de-d537-5aad-887c-c53c5a94b62f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3c/3c17bd753a4a017caea2942fdf2928157a414fd1f4b8bfe4a6274c3a52efb139.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507180} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a964f53-25eb-58dd-8f88-fafa7dd634ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c4c64a2f-c1df-53a5-b259-43fe5b3054cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-102104" :question/problem "Which of the following number lines gives the solution to $-2<\\frac{1-3x}{4}\\le 1?$" :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & <\\frac{1-3x}{4}\\le 1 \\\\ -2\\cdot 4 & <\\frac{1-3x}{4}\\cdot 4\\le 1\\cdot 4 \\\\ -8 & <1-3x\\le 4 \\\\ -8-1 & <1-3x-1\\le 4-1 \\\\ -9 & <-3x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we need to divide by $-3.$ However, because we are dividing by a negative, we also need to flip the inequality signs.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9 & <-3x\\le 3 \\\\ \\frac{-9}{-3} & >\\frac{-3x}{-3}\\ge \\frac{3}{-3} \\\\ 3 & >x\\ge -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution can be written as $3>x\\ge -1$,  but this is somewhat difficult to read because the larger number is on the left rather than the right. So, we will rewrite the solution by reversing the order of the numbers: \n\n$$\n-1\\le x<3\n$$\n\nWe can represent this solution using a number line, as follows.\n\n![](images/3c/3c17bd753a4a017caea2942fdf2928157a414fd1f4b8bfe4a6274c3a52efb139.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507422 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068685 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7229f1d0-4ba7-50ff-b5be-5697c886a175" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Compound Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b094b0a8-72ce-5a2d-bcb9-dc0d69133d30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b094b0a8-72ce-5a2d-bcb9-dc0d69133d30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507066} :answer-field/id #uuid "3817fab8-1016-52b3-bdea-5aae0c544f78" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507270} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b816b4c2-911f-59de-a135-d700453deda1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b816b4c2-911f-59de-a135-d700453deda1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507083} :answer-field/id #uuid "c19e6efe-fc3a-5437-913d-b382a7ea7390" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507360} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3871981b-1eb0-5b69-9c56-0e1751dd91d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3871981b-1eb0-5b69-9c56-0e1751dd91d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506813} :answer-field/id #uuid "f17ffbea-ad40-56c4-b3f5-de225ddcb4fa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507390}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3b28dcca-9835-5578-8d24-be0b3f92933c" :question/math-academy-id "q-214694" :question/problem "Find the solution to the inequality $-1\\le 3x+5\\le 8.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$x\\,\\le $\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition principle, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le 3x+5\\le 8 \\\\ -1-5 & \\le 3x+5-5\\le 8-5 \\\\ -6 & \\le 3x\\le 3 \\\\ \\frac{-6}{3} & \\le \\frac{3x}{3}\\le \\frac{3}{3} \\\\ -2 & \\le x\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-2\\le x\\le 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290305 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068685 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7229f1d0-4ba7-50ff-b5be-5697c886a175" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Compound Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36af17ea-cac8-52c0-92d5-c6ec2922a2c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36af17ea-cac8-52c0-92d5-c6ec2922a2c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288397} :answer-field/id #uuid "1934fb92-eff7-5cc2-80f6-50308250ae74" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289791} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0b2029b-117e-588d-bd5b-c003c19dc8ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0b2029b-117e-588d-bd5b-c003c19dc8ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289104} :answer-field/id #uuid "87e35e52-a33d-50d1-bef6-7023ece73ad3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290026} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29233aa0-7f3f-5ec2-b539-ada9fc07a5a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29233aa0-7f3f-5ec2-b539-ada9fc07a5a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288306} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca53ce72-d828-5a11-a7a5-e42a6dde34c2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "489f31b9-96a3-50ae-87c4-3a1fc2efa912" :question/math-academy-id "q-214755" :question/problem "Find the solution to the inequality $1<\\frac{x+5}{3}\\le 2.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}$\\,x\\le $\n\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual.\n\nFirst, we multiply by $3$ to eliminate the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & <\\frac{x+5}{3}\\le 2 \\\\ 3\\cdot 1 & <3\\cdot \\frac{x+5}{3}\\le 3\\cdot 2 \\\\ 3 & <x+5\\le 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we continue isolating $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & <x+5\\le 6 \\\\ 3-5 & <x+5-5\\le 6-5 \\\\ -2 & <x\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-2<x\\le 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507425 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068686 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5930113e-6971-59c9-810a-97fd25bc4f89" :knowledge-point/title "Compound Inequalities That Require Flipping the Inequality Sign"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d66e4964-a647-5a06-b187-435cbe776716" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d66e4964-a647-5a06-b187-435cbe776716" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507140} :answer-field/id #uuid "a99339ea-5130-5f12-a804-9842b0f7c08e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507347} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0596089-e041-5372-b94c-041a70993db6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0596089-e041-5372-b94c-041a70993db6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507065} :answer-field/id #uuid "e485c39f-dd86-581b-b33c-73fd6b3fb5d7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507379} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d99c7c75-8a46-5e5f-87ad-1726c3ac2be5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507147}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d99c7c75-8a46-5e5f-87ad-1726c3ac2be5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507147} :answer-field/id #uuid "e857517a-1ced-5348-9fbd-4c5b71957e8d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "40ca9940-126e-5709-b31a-f1358dcfed92" :question/math-academy-id "q-214767" :question/problem "Find the solution to the inequality $2\\le -4x+6<10.$\n\n$-1$\n{{field-1}}\n$x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & \\le -4x+6<10 \\\\ 2-6 & \\le -4x+6-6<10-6 \\\\ -4 & \\le -4x<4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $-4.$ Note that since we are dividing by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality signs.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4 & \\le -4x<4 \\\\ \\frac{-4}{-4} & \\ge \\frac{-4x}{-4}>\\frac{4}{-4} \\\\ 1 & \\ge x>-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution can be written as $1\\ge x>-1$, but this is somewhat difficult to read because the larger number is on the left rather than the right. So, we will rewrite the solution by reversing the order of the numbers: \n\nTherefore, the solution is $-1<x\\le 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069228 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068686 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5930113e-6971-59c9-810a-97fd25bc4f89" :knowledge-point/title "Compound Inequalities That Require Flipping the Inequality Sign"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50a61edb-a827-5360-a4a4-72430cd2463f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18<x<3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506861} {:answer/id #uuid "550b441b-3efa-5e9e-9e1f-f7f49ccb951f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3<x<15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506876} {:answer/id #uuid "d947d0e6-9a40-5168-996a-f3ee438e94b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3<x<16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507146} {:answer/id #uuid "da7ea81a-6c3e-5d46-99ca-109614820347" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3<x<18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507150} {:answer/id #uuid "e900a3b8-d179-5b41-b311-f02d66693bd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15<x<3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da7ea81a-6c3e-5d46-99ca-109614820347" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3<x<18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507150} :answer-field/id #uuid "5696f866-cced-54cd-962d-9825c54cd08a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066546}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b61c5dfe-34c0-5830-8c59-cd20d813f4bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-3070" :question/problem "What is the solution to $-10<\\frac{6-2x}{3}<0?$" :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10 & <\\frac{6-2x}{3}<0 \\\\ 3\\cdot (-10) & <3\\cdot (\\frac{6-2x}{3})<3\\cdot 0 \\\\ -30 & <6-2x<0 \\\\ -30-6 & <6-2x-6<0-6 \\\\ -36 & <-2x<-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we need to divide by $-2.$ However, because we are dividing by a negative, we also need to flip the inequality signs.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-36 & <-2x<-6 \\\\ \\frac{-36}{-2} & >\\frac{-2x}{-2}>\\frac{-6}{-2} \\\\ 18 & >x>3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution can be written as $18>x>3,$ but this is somewhat difficult to read because the larger number is on the left rather than the right. So, we will rewrite the solution by reversing the order of the numbers:\n\n$$\n3<x<18\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507522 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068687 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3ff37f0-6e45-5da4-ac87-1b93c8df3e80" :knowledge-point/title "Representing Solutions of Compound Inequalities on Number Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bd89293-7162-5f72-a547-f513956767f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/76/76d9d3a567556395ade541cc221e34f8be01a673a3bbd2a5665ada9816f5b7c6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506697} {:answer/id #uuid "3660ae55-222d-572d-af2a-1eaeb22f7d22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d6/d62e205d0ecd52caf22489fa18279a6c7aa28e4be7edbd04b2ef9b7993801987.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506809} {:answer/id #uuid "a8263c8e-8441-59e6-bed0-8bda2ff3a21e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/94/94de2b57de157f66466c49fcccb3ac0566673dc403a124e9c75fb0d681d8183a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507045} {:answer/id #uuid "c78f074b-64b9-56c6-b131-2bfdbcde59ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a3/a3f429bdca3524e740a3978168d4e0343473d8a896fc173d35d9da0f952ff513.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507112} {:answer/id #uuid "c8fc281e-d26d-5d07-ab2f-6d54ef0128d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/08/0831f52dd88060c2a52a85369203bc86677dc63bd8c166060854a1bc3a17fc1c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8fc281e-d26d-5d07-ab2f-6d54ef0128d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/08/0831f52dd88060c2a52a85369203bc86677dc63bd8c166060854a1bc3a17fc1c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507115} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ed705f3-8758-5969-aca2-668713927df9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507260}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e50c909d-a5a1-584e-97a8-2de3d20d9c6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-44762" :question/problem "Which of the following number lines gives the solution to $-13\\le -5x+2\\le -8?$" :question/worked-solution "We isolate $x$  by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual.\n\nFirst, we apply the addition principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-13 & \\le -5x+2\\le -8 \\\\ -13-2 & \\le -5x+2-2\\le -8-2 \\\\ -15 & \\le -5x\\le -10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $-5.$ Note that since we are dividing by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality signs. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-15 & \\le -5x\\le -10 \\\\ \\frac{-15}{-5} & \\ge \\frac{-5x}{-5}\\ge \\frac{-10}{-5} \\\\ 3 & \\ge x\\ge 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution can be written as $3\\ge x\\ge 2$, but this is somewhat difficult to read because the larger number is on the left rather than the right. So, we will rewrite the solution by reversing the order of the numbers: \n\n$$\n2\\le x\\le 3.\n$$\n\nWe can represent this solution using a number line, as follows.  \n\n![](images/08/0831f52dd88060c2a52a85369203bc86677dc63bd8c166060854a1bc3a17fc1c.png)"}]}
